So anyway, so again,

02:48:08.059 --> 02:48:09.920
you have to do, again, the spellchecking process.

02:48:10.200 --> 02:48:13.100
Maybe later on, you wanted to do automatic backup.

02:48:13.860 --> 02:48:15.920
Maybe you want to do automatic spellchecking.

02:48:16.039 --> 02:48:19.520
But then how do you write inside one single process,

02:48:19.899 --> 02:48:22.639
how do you make sure the user can still type in stuff

02:48:22.639 --> 02:48:25.659
while those other functions of your program

02:48:25.659 --> 02:48:29.920
happen at the same time. Now, these functions can be implemented

02:48:29.920 --> 02:48:33.840
since we have this notion of multi-processing. A processor can execute

02:48:33.840 --> 02:48:37.920
multiple processes simultaneously. What we can do is maybe

02:48:37.920 --> 02:48:41.760
instead of creating only one process for the Microsoft Word application

02:48:41.760 --> 02:48:45.920
we create three processes. One process is responsible for writing data

02:48:45.920 --> 02:48:49.840
one process is responsible for doing the spell checking and one

02:48:49.840 --> 02:48:53.139
