02:48:53.139 --> 02:49:02.719
But the problem is, because operating systems were designed to run processes in a way where

02:49:02.719 --> 02:49:07.399
they're isolated from each other, they now had to break that isolation.

02:49:07.399 --> 02:49:11.500
Because the process that was being backed up had to have access to the data, but the

02:49:11.500 --> 02:49:17.239
process that was reading the input from the user, the spell checking also had to have

02:49:17.239 --> 02:49:22.459
access to the data, and this became very problematic to do it by using the processes.

02:49:22.459 --> 02:49:24.599
So then people needed a different mechanism

02:49:24.599 --> 02:49:26.419
that made it a little bit easier

02:49:26.419 --> 02:49:29.399
to implement multiple functionalities

02:49:29.399 --> 02:49:31.000
inside one application

02:49:31.000 --> 02:49:35.399
